e exactly\0awhat the real call's own arguments of the same names expect -- all three are now solved via\0a`MarketPool.keep_yt_split` against the pool's raw reserve ratio (the ratio `add_liquidity`'s\0aproportional deposit actually targets), not `zap_swap_amount`'s curve-swap ratio, which a\0alater integration review found recommended the wrong split and left SY stranded. `lp_estimate`\0apreviews `add_liquidity`'s own `lp_minted` using the same `(pt_desired * total_lp /\0apt_reserve).min(sy_desired * total_lp / sy_reserve)` formula -- like every quote in this\0aprotocol, exact only if reserves/`total_lp` do not move between this read and the real call.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bKeepYtQuote\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0blp_estimate\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bmint_amount\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\13mint_fee_underlying\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0apt_desired\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0asy_desired\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06yt_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\01GPermissionless keeper call: extend this contract's *instance* storage (admin, config,\0areserves, totals, settlement rate, fee buckets) for ~30 days. Soroban does not bump instance\0aTTL on ordinary reads or writes, so a long-dated market needs this called periodically (or\0aan archived instance restored) -- see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.\00\00\00\00\04bump\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cKeepYtResult\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09lp_minted\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07pt_used\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07sy_used\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09yt_minted\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cRedeemResult\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12underlying_from_pt\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12underlying_from_yt\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06market\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\