out = 0`); `min_pt_out` protects the whole round trip.\00\00\00\0dwrap_and_mint\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_pt_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aMintResult\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eswap_pt_for_sy\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05pt_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_sy_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eswap_sy_for_pt\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_pt_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00**Flash-mint** buy of YT. Tokenizes `sy_in` SY into PT + YT, sells all of the PT back into\0athe pool in the same transaction, and leaves the user with the YT plus the SY the PT\0afetched. Net cost of the YT is `sy_in - sy_back` SY. Returns `(yt_out, sy_back)`.\0a\0a`pt_in` is a caller-supplied literal (quoted off-chain the same way `PrincipalManager.mint`\0acomputes `pt_minted`: tokenization fee withheld, then valued at the live oracle rate --\0ae.g. via `MarketPool.quote_sy_for_yt(sy_in).yt_out`, which replicates that exact formula),\0a**not** derived from `mint`'s return value -- chaining `minted.pt_minted` straight into\0a`swap_pt_for_sy`'s authorized call has exactly the `Error(Auth, InvalidAction)` drift risk\0athe module docs describe, since `mint`'s output depends on the live oracle rate. If `pt_in`\0adoesn't match what `mint` actually produced, `swap_pt_for_sy`'s own balance check simply\0afails closed (an ordinary revert, not an auth error); a caller can never benefit from\0aquoting `pt_in` higher than the real `pt_minted`\00\00\00\0eswap_sy_for_yt\00\00\00\00\00\07\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05pt_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_yt_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cmax_net_cost\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\a8**Flash-redeem** sale of YT: the pool recombines the YT with PT from its own reserve and\0apays the difference in SY. Returns the SY received; reverts below `min_sy_out`.\00\00\00\0eswap_yt_for_sy\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05yt_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_sy_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0etransfer_admin\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dcurrent_admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09new_admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\91Register a market by its pool, after checking that the pool, its manager and the tokens the\0apool trades all describe the same market. Admin-only.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fregister_market\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aMarketInfo\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10remove_liquidity\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05lp_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_pt_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_sy_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00M`FlashMintQuote` restated in underlying units, for `quote_underlying_for_yt`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\18UnderlyingFlashMintQuote\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\13mint_fee_underlying\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\13swap_fee_underlying\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0funderlying_back\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06yt_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\97Remove a market from the registry (a mistaken or retired listing). Admin-only; users can no\0alonger route through it, existing positions are unaffected.\00\00\00\00\11unregister_market\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00*PT and/or YT -> underlying after maturity.\00\00\00\00\00\12redeem_at_maturity\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09pt_amount\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09yt_amount\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0cRedeemResult\00\00\00\01\00\00\01\f7Preview for `add_liquidity_single_underlying`. `sy_in` is exactly the value to pass as the\0areal call's own `sy_in` argument (quoted via `SYWrapper.exchange_rate()`, the same conversion\0aevery other `_for_underlying`/`_single_underlying` quote in this Router uses); `pt_used`,\0a`sy_used` and `lp_minted` preview `MarketPool.add_liquidity_single_sy`'s own return exactly\0a(`MarketPool.quote_add_liquidity_single_sy`). Found missing in a dApp-integration review (\22no\0aquote for the two new USDY LP functions\22).\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\1aSingleSidedUnderlyingQuote\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09lp_minted\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07pt_used\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07sy_used\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Pendle's \22keep YT\22 deposit: `underlying_amount` of underlying becomes LP *and* YT, with no\0aswap and so no price-impact slippage (the only guard that applies is `min_lp_out`, exactly\0aas `add_liquidity`'s own proportional deposit already works). Wraps to SY, mints PT+YT from\0a`mint_amount` of it, then adds PT and SY as a normal proportional deposit -- keeping the YT\0ainstead of selling it, which is the one difference from `add_liquidity_single_sy`.\0a\0a`mint_amount`, `pt_desired` and `sy_desired` are all plain arguments, computed off-chain\0a(quote `MarketPool.keep_yt_split` and `reserves()`/`lp_total_supply()` -- or just call\0a`quote_add_liquidity_keep_yt`, which does exactly that -- before building this call, the\0asame way every other min-out in this Router is quoted beforehand) rather than anything\0athis function derives mid-execution. That distinction matters: an earlier version derived\0a`sy_remaining` from `deposit`'s live-exchange-rate-dependent output and `pt_desired` from\0a`mint`'s live-oracle-rate-dependent output\00\00\00\15add_liquidity_keep_yt\00\00\00\00\00\00\08\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11underlying_amount\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bmint_amount\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0apt_desired\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0asy_desired\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_lp_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0cKeepYtResult\00\00\00\00\00\00\02-Preview `remove_liquidity_to_underlying`. Named `quote_lp_to_underlying` -- the full\0afunction name with a `quote_` prefix is 36 bytes, over Soroban's 32-byte export-name cap.\0aEntirely delegated to `MarketPool.quote_lp_exit` (the proportional split and the PT-sale\0apricing both live there, since the sale must be priced against the reserves *after* the\0asplit, not before it -- a first version of this quote got that wrong, pricing the sale\0aagainst pre-removal reserves and overstating the real payout); this function only adds\0athe underlying-unit conversion.\00\00\00\00\00\00\16quote_lp_to_underlying\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05lp_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\1eRemoveLiquidityUnderlyingQuote\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00PT -> SY (`MarketPool`) -> underlying (`SYWrapper.withdraw_gained`), in one transaction.\0aThe swap leg is unguarded; `min_underlying_out` protects the whole round trip at the\0afinal, underlying-denominated output -- the same reasoning `swap_underlying_for_pt` uses\0ain reverse.\0a\0aReads `baseline = from`'s SY balance *before* the swap, then unwraps only what the swap\0agained (`withdraw_gained`) rather than sweeping `from`'s entire SY balance\0a(`withdraw_all`) -- a caller who already held unrelated SY no longer needs to clear it\0afirst. The swap's SY payout is a curve-derived amount that can drift by a few raw units\0abetween simulation and real execution, so a plain `withdraw` reverted `Error(Auth,\0aInvalidAction)` live on Testnet while this function was first written -- confirmed in\0a`docs/DAPP_SMART_CONTRACT_INTEGRATION_GUIDE.md`. `withdraw_gained` reads the balance at\0aexecution time instead, so there is nothing curve-derived left in the authorized\0ainvocation. An earlier version used `withdraw_all` and a zero-pre-existi\00\00\00\16swap_pt_for_underlying\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05pt_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12min_underlying_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\e1Underlying -> SY (`SYWrapper.deposit`) -> PT (`MarketPool`), in one transaction and one\0asignature, for a user who holds the underlying rather than SY. The wrap leg is unguarded\0a(`min_shares_out = 0`); `min_pt_out` protects the whole round trip, matching\0a`wrap_and_mint`'s existing pattern of guarding only the final output.\0a\0a`sy_in` is a caller-supplied literal (quote `SYWrapper.exchange_rate()` off-chain, the same\0aconvention `add_liquidity_single_underlying` and `wrap_and_mint` use for their own `sy_in`),\0a**not** derived from `deposit`'s return value -- chaining `deposit`'s live-rate-dependent\0aoutput straight into `swap_sy_for_pt`'s authorized call has exactly the `Error(Auth,\0aInvalidAction)` drift risk the module docs describe.\00\00\00\00\00\00\16swap_underlying_for_pt\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11underlying_amount\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_pt_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Same flash-mint as `swap_sy_for_yt`, but for a caller who holds the underlying rather than\0aSY: wraps `underlying_amount` into SY first, runs the identical flash-mint, then unwraps\0athe SY the PT sale fetched back into underlying, so the whole round trip -- pay underlying,\0areceive YT plus underlying change -- is one transaction and one signature. The pool never\0aadvances anything: `from` still needs `underlying_amount` in hand up front, exactly as\0a`swap_sy_for_yt` needs `sy_in` up front (see the Router's module docs on why this is not a\0atrue flash loan).\0a\0a`sy_in` is a caller-supplied literal (quote `SYWrapper.exchange_rate()` off-chain:\0a`underlying_amount * RATE_SCALE / exchange_rate()`, matching `SYWrapper.deposit`'s own\0arounding), **not** derived from `deposit`'s return value -- a later integration review\0afound that chaining `deposit`'s live-rate-dependent output straight into `mint`'s\0aauthorized call had exactly the `Error(Auth, InvalidAction)` drift risk the Router's\0amodule docs describe, just not yet fixed \00\00\00\16swap_underlying_for_yt\00\00\00\00\00\08\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11underlying_amount\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05pt_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_yt_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cmax_net_cost\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\01;Same flash-redeem as `swap_yt_for_sy`, but unwraps the SY proceeds into underlying in the\0asame transaction, for a caller who wants to receive the underlying directly. Reads\0a`baseline = from`'s SY balance before the swap, then unwraps only the gain\0a(`withdraw_gained`) -- see `swap_pt_for_underlying`'s docs for why.\00\00\00\00\16swap_yt_for_underlying\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05yt_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12min_underlying_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\02\04Preview for `remove_liquidity_to_underlying`. `pt_out`/`sy_out` are `remove_liquidity`'s own\0aproportional split for `lp_in`; `underlying_out` previews the whole round trip (selling the\0aPT leg via `MarketPool.quote_lp_exit`, which correctly prices that sale against the reserves\0a*after* the removal, not before it, then unwrapping everything via\0a`SYWrapper.exchange_rate()`) -- the value to compare `min_underlying_out` against. Found\0amissing in the same dApp-integration review as `SingleSidedUnderlyingQuote` above.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\1eRemoveLiquidityUnderlyingQuote\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06pt_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fswap_fee_shares\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06sy_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eunderlying_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\17add_liquidity_single_sy\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_lp_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\eePreview `swap_pt_for_underlying`: `MarketPool.quote_pt_for_sy`'s SY-denominated\0a`amount_out`/`fee_shares`, both converted to underlying via the same `exchange_rate()`\0aread `SYWrapper.withdraw_all` would apply to the swap's real SY payout.\00\00\00\00\00\17quote_pt_for_underlying\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05pt_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0fUnderlyingQuote\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01.Preview `swap_underlying_for_pt`. `amount_out` is PT (unaffected by the wrap leg);\0a`fee_shares` is the AMM swap fee, in SY, exactly as `MarketPool.quote_sy_for_pt` reports it\0a-- there is nothing to convert on the output side, only the input (`underlying_amount` ->\0aSY shares) feeds into the pool quote.\00\00\00\00\00\17quote_underlying_for_pt\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11underlying_amount\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\05Quote\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\f4Preview `swap_underlying_for_yt`: wraps `underlying_amount` to SY shares, previews the\0aflash-mint via `MarketPool.quote_sy_for_yt`, then converts `sy_back` and both fee legs to\0aunderlying the same way the real call's final `withdraw_all` would.\00\00\00\17quote_underlying_for_yt\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11underlying_amount\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\18UnderlyingFlashMintQuote\00\00\00\00\00\00\00xPreview `swap_yt_for_underlying`: `MarketPool.quote_yt_for_sy`'s SY-denominated payout and\0afee, converted to underlying.\00\00\00\17quote_yt_for_underlying\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05yt_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0fUnderlyingQuote\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\bbPreview `add_liquidity_keep_yt`. Returns the exact `mint_amount` to pass into that call\0a(the SY split `MarketPool.zap_swap_amount` recommends for `underlying_amount`'s worth of\0awrapped shares), the SY left over for the proportional deposit leg, and the YT the mint\0aalone would produce (via `MarketPool.quote_sy_for_yt`'s mint leg -- its sell-PT leg is\0airrelevant here since this flow deposits the minted PT as liquidity instead of selling it).\00\00\00\00\1bquote_add_liquidity_keep_yt\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11underlying_amount\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0bKeepYtQuote\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Same true flash-mint as `flash_mint_yt`, for a caller who holds the underlying rather than\0aSY. Wraps `underlying_budget` of underlying into SY first -- not the full `sy_in` notional,\0asince the whole point of this function is that the caller never needs the full notional --\0aso `from`'s SY balance covers whatever the real net cost turns out to be, as long as the\0acaller chose `underlying_budget` generously enough to cover `max_net_cost` SY shares at the\0acurrent `SYWrapper.exchange_rate()` (a plain off-chain conversion, the same kind every other\0a`_for_underlying` caller already does). `max_net_cost` is SY-denominated and passed through\0ato the pool unchanged -- kept as its own parameter, not derived from `underlying_budget`,\0abecause the two are only numerically equal while `exchange_rate()` is exactly 1.0 (true for\0aevery `SYWrapper` deployed today, not guaranteed forever; see `docs/ROUTER_QUOTES.md` \c2\a72).\0a\0aAny surplus (`underlying_budget` wrapped minus the real net cost) is unwrapped back to\0aunderlying before this\00\00\00\1dflash_mint_yt_from_underlying\00\00\00\00\00\00\08\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_yt_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cmax_net_cost\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11underlying_budget\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\13min_underlying_back\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\01JPreview `add_liquidity_single_underlying`. Named `quote_add_liquidity_underlying`, not\0athe full function name with \22single\22 in it too -- Soroban caps exported function names\0aat 32 bytes, and `quote_add_liquidity_single_underlying` is 37. No ambiguity results:\0a`add_liquidity_keep_yt`'s own quote already has its own distinct name.\00\00\00\00\00\1equote_add_liquidity_underlying\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11underlying_amount\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\1aSingleSidedUnderlyingQuote\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00LP -> PT + SY (`MarketPool.remove_liquidity`) -> sell the PT leg for SY\0a(`MarketPool.swap_gained_pt_for_sy`) -> unwrap to underlying (`SYWrapper.withdraw_gained`),\0ain one transaction and one signature -- found missing in an integration review (landing in\0aunderlying previously needed 2-3 separate calls: remove, sell the PT, unwrap).\0a\0aReads `baseline_pt`/`baseline_sy` -- `from`'s PT and SY balances *before* `remove_liquidity`\0a-- then sells and unwraps only what this call itself produced on top of those, via\0a`swap_gained_pt_for_sy`/`withdraw_gained`, rather than chaining `remove_liquidity`'s PT/SY\0apayout straight into further authorized calls as explicit arguments -- see the module\0adocs. An earlier version used the full-sweep primitives (`swap_all_pt_for_sy`,\0a`withdraw_all`) with a zero-pre-existing-balance precondition instead; the dApp team found\0athis failed routinely, since both the \22LP only\22 zap and Keep YT deposits can themselves\0aleave small PT/SY remainders in `from`'s wallet, and simply having bought PT o\00\00\00\1eremove_liquidity_to_underlying\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05lp_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12min_underlying_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\feUnderlying -> SY (`SYWrapper.deposit`) -> single-sided LP deposit (`MarketPool\0a.add_liquidity_single_sy`), in one transaction and one signature, for a user who holds\0athe underlying rather than SY -- found missing in an integration review (single-sided LP\0afrom underlying previously needed a separate `deposit` first, two signatures).\0a\0a`sy_in` is a caller-supplied literal (quote `SYWrapper.exchange_rate()` off-chain, the\0asame `underlying_amount * RATE_SCALE / exchange_rate()` used throughout this Router), not\0aderived from `deposit`'s return value, for the same reason `swap_underlying_for_yt` takes\0a`sy_in` as an argument rather than deriving it -- see the module docs. The wrap leg is\0aunguarded (`min_shares_out = 0`); `min_lp_out` protects the whole round trip.\00\00\00\00\00\1fadd_liquidity_single_underlying\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11underlying_amount\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05sy_in\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amin_lp_out\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\0b")
  (@custom "contractenvmetav0" (after data) "\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\1a\00\00\00\00")
  (@custom "contractmetav0" (after data) "\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05rsver\00\00\00\00\00\00\061.94.1\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08rssdkver\00\00\00/26.0.1#f52b6aad85f18c5e312ff3f60e57cb613274e6bb\00")
)
